---
// Generated from the live WordPress page, then tidied by hand where needed.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RegularsSignup from '../components/RegularsSignup.astro';
---

<Layout title="Roadmap - clamcentral.com">
	<main class="px-4 pt-12 pb-20" style="background: #ffffff">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-[1038px]">
			<h1 style="font-size:clamp(35px, 3.64vw, 51px);line-height:1.00;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:16px">Development Roadmap</h1>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>Bible Learning Activities Packs • NEW!</strong></h2>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">I have 800+ Bible Learning Activities (BLAs), many should work great with just about any lesson in the Sunday School curriculum you are using right now. Even the best curriculum has some clinkers now and then. These BLAs are curated, categorized, designed to be fun and biblically profound. Lots are available now and many more are arriving soon. The CLAMcentral Regulars Newsletter will keep you updated.</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>PS: The activities are from the CLAMbake lessons, but all references to CLAMbake have been removed.</strong> <strong>These activities really are intended to be used with any Sunday School curriculum!</strong></p>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>The CLAMcentral Ministries Channel</strong></h2>
			<h3 style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>The 3-Steps to Lifelong Discipleship Project • Countless hours of useful, practical content.</strong></h3>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">Wait--<strong>CLAMcentral Ministries?</strong> Is this a NEW channel? Nope. I started it in 2009--wow! I've ignored it for years now, but it's got one thing I really like: The CLAMcentral Ministries title.</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">Here's what's coming up there:</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>Step 1. The Kids Ministry Toolbox</strong> will soon enter an <strong>update</strong> cycle, adding more articles relevant to ministry leaders and teachers. Helpful videos as well.</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>Step 2. CLAMbake Curriculum.</strong> The Old Testament is completely done, the New Testament is being released a step at a time. The navbar at the top of most pages has links to both the Old and New Testament lessons. <strong>The New Testament will be concluded near the end of 2026 or shortly thereafter.</strong></p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>Step 3. Kids Party.</strong> This highly successful ministry is <strong>completely done</strong> and available now. Kids Party is designed to draw kids and families into your fellowship.</p>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>The Sunday School Channel </strong></h2>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">This channel is about to be revamped. Most of the current videos will be transferred to the CLAMcentral channel, replaced instead by videos dedicated pretty much fully to the <strong>Bible Learning Activities Packs</strong> that I feel will become an important part of CLAMcentral.</p>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>Pastor Dain Spore </strong></h2>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>Pastor Dain is CLAMcentral's resident sounding board and cheerleader. </strong>He will be taking virtually all of the CLAMbake Bible stories, using them as launching pads for video devotionals to inspire Sunday School teachers as they prepare for their next class. We've already shot seven videos that I will post in the near future.</p>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>CLAMcentral Community</strong></h2>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>As they say, the wave of the future is here now. </strong>Websites--such as this one--are now "old news." The latest thing is community groups. I love the idea of live group gatherings to find solutions, share insights, make known the things God is doing in our churches and Children's Ministries, and the like. If you'd like to know more about online communities, I'll be purchasing (God allowing, of course) <a href="https://circle.so/"><strong>Circle.so</strong></a> software. Don't let the "A new era for digital businesses" headline scare you--scroll down their page to learn the very cool features.</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>It's something to pray about!</strong></p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">God's blessings,</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>Tom Finley</strong></p>
		</div>
	</main>
	<RegularsSignup heading="Grab my NEWSLETTER!" perks={["Follow the progress of the HUGE <strong>3-Steps to Discipleship</strong> program that rapidly accelerates the success of your ministry.", "Be the first to know about<strong> this and other </strong><strong>new resources</strong> as they arrive.", "The newsletter is sent to your email address <strong>once a month</strong> (more or less predictably!)"]} sectionBg="#ffffff" />
</Layout>
